# Strict Modular Monolith Rules

1. Modules live only under `src/modules/<moduleName>`.
2. A module may expose behavior to other modules only through `public.js`.
3. Cross-module imports into `controllers`, `services`, `repositories`, `models`, `routes`, or `dtos` are forbidden.
4. Shared infrastructure belongs under `src/config`, `src/middlewares`, or future `src/shared`.
5. Controllers handle HTTP concerns only and delegate business logic to services.
6. Services own use-case orchestration and may depend on repositories inside the same module.
7. Repositories are the only layer that should directly query Mongoose models.
8. Routes may import only their module controllers and shared middleware.
9. Background jobs must be created through `src/config/queue.js`.
10. Configuration must be loaded through `src/config/index.js`; do not read `process.env` throughout feature code.
